# The first module of the stage0 sample `modules`: rectangles, what kind of
# rectangle one is, and a constant and a record whose names the module after
# it also uses for things of its own.
shapes is module
shapes purpose "Rectangles, their areas and kinds, for the app module to use"
shapes path shapes
shapes imports standard.math
shapes imports standard.compare
shapes imports standard.test
shapes exports Kind
shapes exports Rectangle
shapes exports Label
shapes exports area
shapes exports kindOf
shapes exports sideCount

Kind is enum
Kind purpose "Whether a rectangle's sides are all the same length"
Kind typeParameter none
Kind variant square none
Kind variant oblong none

Rectangle is record
Rectangle purpose "A rectangle's width and height"
Rectangle typeParameter none
Rectangle field width Int64
Rectangle field height Int64

Label is record
Label purpose "A name shapes gives a rectangle"
Label typeParameter none
Label field text String

sides is constant
sides purpose "How many sides a rectangle has"
sides type Int64
sides value 4

area is operation
area purpose "A rectangle's area"
area invariant multipliesSides "\"The area is the width times the height\""
area typeParameter none
area input shape Rectangle copied
area output Int64
area outputOwnedBy none
area raises none
area effect none
area uses none
area memoryHeap false
area async false
area maxRecursion none
area label begin loopKind none
area label begin within none
area let none
area at begin do readWidth
area at begin do readHeight
area at begin do multiply
area at begin return ok product

readWidth is call
readWidth in area
readWidth invokes Rectangle.width
readWidth argument record Rectangle shape copy
readWidth result width Int64
readWidth ownedBy none
readWidth cleanedBy none
readWidth borrows none
readWidth catch none
readWidth suppresses none

readHeight is call
readHeight in area
readHeight invokes Rectangle.height
readHeight argument record Rectangle shape copy
readHeight result height Int64
readHeight ownedBy none
readHeight cleanedBy none
readHeight borrows none
readHeight catch none
readHeight suppresses none

multiply is call
multiply in area
multiply invokes math.multiplyInt64
multiply argument left Int64 width copy
multiply argument right Int64 height copy
multiply result product Int64
multiply ownedBy none
multiply cleanedBy none
multiply borrows none
multiply catch none
multiply suppresses none

kindOf is operation
kindOf purpose "Whether a rectangle is a square or an oblong"
kindOf invariant comparesSides "\"A rectangle whose width is its height is a square; any other is an oblong\""
kindOf typeParameter none
kindOf input shape Rectangle copied
kindOf output Kind
kindOf outputOwnedBy none
kindOf raises none
kindOf effect none
kindOf uses none
kindOf memoryHeap false
kindOf async false
kindOf maxRecursion none
kindOf label begin loopKind none
kindOf label begin within none
kindOf label square loopKind none
kindOf label square within none
kindOf label oblong loopKind none
kindOf label oblong within none
kindOf let none
kindOf at begin do readWidth
kindOf at begin do readHeight
kindOf at begin do sameCheck
kindOf at begin branch if same goto square else goto oblong
kindOf at square do makeSquare
kindOf at square return ok squareKind
kindOf at oblong do makeOblong
kindOf at oblong return ok oblongKind

readWidth is call
readWidth in kindOf
readWidth invokes Rectangle.width
readWidth argument record Rectangle shape copy
readWidth result width Int64
readWidth ownedBy none
readWidth cleanedBy none
readWidth borrows none
readWidth catch none
readWidth suppresses none

readHeight is call
readHeight in kindOf
readHeight invokes Rectangle.height
readHeight argument record Rectangle shape copy
readHeight result height Int64
readHeight ownedBy none
readHeight cleanedBy none
readHeight borrows none
readHeight catch none
readHeight suppresses none

sameCheck is call
sameCheck in kindOf
sameCheck invokes compare.equalInt64
sameCheck argument left Int64 width copy
sameCheck argument right Int64 height copy
sameCheck result same Bool
sameCheck ownedBy none
sameCheck cleanedBy none
sameCheck borrows none
sameCheck catch none
sameCheck suppresses none

makeSquare is call
makeSquare in kindOf
makeSquare invokes Kind.square
makeSquare argument none
makeSquare result squareKind Kind
makeSquare ownedBy none
makeSquare cleanedBy none
makeSquare borrows none
makeSquare catch none
makeSquare suppresses none

makeOblong is call
makeOblong in kindOf
makeOblong invokes Kind.oblong
makeOblong argument none
makeOblong result oblongKind Kind
makeOblong ownedBy none
makeOblong cleanedBy none
makeOblong borrows none
makeOblong catch none
makeOblong suppresses none

sideCount is operation
sideCount purpose "How many sides a rectangle has: this module's constant `sides`"
sideCount invariant countsSides "\"Gives the module's own constant: a rectangle has 4 sides\""
sideCount typeParameter none
sideCount input none
sideCount output Int64
sideCount outputOwnedBy none
sideCount raises none
sideCount effect none
sideCount uses none
sideCount memoryHeap false
sideCount async false
sideCount maxRecursion none
sideCount label begin loopKind none
sideCount label begin within none
sideCount let none
sideCount at begin return ok sides
